# Freetter Development Guidelines

## Overview

Freetter is a modular Laravel application organized by bounded contexts under `app-modules/`.

## Architecture

- Keep business logic in the owning module.
- Avoid cross-module coupling unless the boundary is explicit and justified.
- Prefer focused changes that preserve existing public behavior.

## Validation

- Run targeted validation for changed behavior.
- Prefer feature tests for request-to-domain behavior.
- Review migrations carefully before accepting schema changes.

## Development A2A Scope

- The repository uses agent-to-agent style handoffs only for development orchestration in VS Code.
- Supported development flow: `freetter-planner` -> `freetter-implementer` -> `freetter-guardian` -> `freetter-release-manager`.
- This does not imply runtime A2A protocol support in Laravel.
- Do not introduce runtime Laravel AI agents, remote agent cards, or A2A production infrastructure unless explicitly requested.

## Sources Of Truth

- Use `/.context` documents for business language and strategic context when needed.
- Before implementation, prioritize `/.context/PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE.md`, `/.context/USE_CASES.md`, `/.context/ENTITIES.md`, and the relevant domain analysis document.
- Keep module ownership and naming aligned with the existing domain structure.
- When implementing Laravel code, use Laravel Boost documentation and tooling first when applicable.

